e z-0 flex max-w-full"><div id="code-block-viewer" dir="ltr" class="q9tKkq_viewer cm-editor z-10 light:cm-light dark:cm-light flex h-full w-full flex-col items-stretch ͼd ͼr"><div class="cm-scroller"><pre class="cm-content q9tKkq_readonly m-0"><code><span># Lab 01 – VHDL Introduction</span><br><br><span>## Exercise 02: 1-bit Half Adder</span><br><br><span>This lab implements and simulates a 1-bit Half Adder using VHDL and ModelSim.</span><br><br><span>## Half Adder Logic</span><br><br><span>A Half Adder has two inputs and two outputs.</span><br><br><span>### Inputs</span><br><span>- A</span><br><span>- B</span><br><br><span>### Outputs</span><br><span>- SUM</span><br><span>- CARRY</span><br><br><span>### Equations</span><br><br><span>SUM = A XOR B  </span><br><span>CARRY = A AND B</span><br><br><span>## Truth Table</span><br><br><span>| A | B | SUM | CARRY |</span><br><span>|---|---|-----|-------|</span><br><span>| 0 | 0 | 0   | 0     |</span><br><span>| 0 | 1 | 1   | 0     |</span><br><span>| 1 | 0 | 1   | 0     |</span><br><span>| 1 | 1 | 0   | 1     |</span><br><br><span>## Tools Used</span><br><br><span>- VHDL</span><br><span>- ModelSim Intel FPGA Edition</span><br><span>- Quartus Prime Lite</span><br><br><span>## Simulation Result</span><br><br><span>The design was compiled successfully and tested using waveform simulation.  </span><br><span>The output follows the expected Half Adder truth table.</span><br><br><span>## Files</span><br><br><span>- `half_adder.vhd` – VHDL design file</span><br><span>- `half_adder_tb.vhd` – Testbench file</span><br><span>- `screenshots/` – Compile and waveform simulation screenshots</span></code></pre></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class=""><div class="" style="width: 100%; transform: none;"></div></div></div></div></div></pre>
